  "result": "I withdrew span `u4` as an `atom` gap rather than revising the record, so this law stays blocked until the operator decides the gap.\n\n**Why it can't be re-mapped:** `u4` sets a condition on when the duty arises. Through `u5`, it requires the approaching vehicle to show \"at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front.\" The ontology's `sig.warning_lamp` does record which way a lamp faces (front, rear or side), but the formulas Core can evaluate only read a lamp's colour and mode. So the rule could only say \"a red flashing lamp is lit, facing any way.\" That is weaker than the law: a vehicle with a flashing red lamp only at its rear would also trigger the duty. The rules forbid weakening a condition, and no neighbouring atom stands in for the lamp's facing:\n- `rel.visible` relates two road users' bodies, not a lamp.\n- `rel.bearing` only places the subject ahead of the approaching vehicle.\n\n**What the gap asks for:** Core needs a way for formulas to read a lamp's facing, for example `sig_warning_lamp [x, colour, mode, facing]`. Once that exists, the record as planned codes unchanged. The coder's second gate run already passed with every other element written.\n\nThe withdrawal is in `record.jsonl`.",
